hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"846","Usama ibn Zayd reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, arrived at a gathering which included 'Abdullah\nibn Ubayy ibn Salul before 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy had become Muslim. He said,\n\Do not bother us in our gathering.\"" The Prophet"
"847","The Prophet would enter upon us, and I had a young brother who was called Abu 'Umair, and he had a pet that would play with him. It died, and the Prophet entered upon us and found him grief-stricken. He asked, ""What's wrong with him?"" He was told, ""His pet has died."" He said, ""O Abu 'Umair, what has befallen the pet?"""
"848","'Alqama said, \'Abdullah gave me a kunya before I had a child.\"""""
"849","'Alqama said, \'Abdullah gave me a kunya before I had a child.\"""""
"850","'A'isha said, \I went to the Prophet"
"851","Our father Musa narrated to us, saying: Our father Wuhayb narrated to us, saying: Our father Hisham narrated to us, from 'Abbad bin Hamzah bin 'Abdullah bin az-Zubayr, that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: ""O Prophet of Allah, do not leave me behind!"" He said: ""Take care of your son, meaning 'Abdullah bin az-Zubayr, so she was known as Umm 'Abdullah."""
"852","Sahl ibn Sa'd related that the name which 'Ali, may Allah be pleased\nwith him, liked best was Abu Turab and that he was happy when he was called\nthat. Only the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, called\nhim that. One day 'Ali was cross with Fatima and went out and reclined\nagainst the wall of the mosque. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, came to look for him and was told that he was leaning against\nthe wall. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, went up\nto him and found that his back was covered with dust. The Prophet, may\nAllah bless him and grant him peace, began to wipe the dust off his back\nand said, 'Sit down Abu Turab (father of dust)!'\""853"""
"853","Abu Mu'ammar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, who said: While the Prophet ﷺ was in a palm grove of ours — a palm grove of Abu Talhah — he relieved himself. Bilal was walking behind him, honoring the Prophet ﷺ by not walking beside him. The Prophet ﷺ passed by a grave and stood until Bilal caught up to him. He said: ""Woe to you, O Bilal! Do you hear what I hear?"" He said: ""I hear nothing."" He said: ""The occupant of this grave is being punished."" He was found to be a Jew."
"854","Qays said, \I heard Mu'awiya say to a young brother of his"
"855","Musa ibn 'Ali reported from his father that 'Amr ibn al-'As said,\n\When you have a lot of close friends"
"856","Khalid ibn Kaysan said, \I was with Ibn 'Umar when Iyyas ibn Khaythama\ngot up and said to him"
"857","Mutarrif said, \I accompanied 'Imran ibn Husayn from Kufa to Basra.\nVery rarely did he arrive at my house without reciting some poetry to me.\nHe said"
"858","Ubayy ibn Ka'b mentioned that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, said, \There is some wisdom in poetry.\"""""
"859","Al-Aswad ibn Suray' said, \Messenger of Allah"
